\end{aligned}
where $\alpha(x)$ and $\beta(x)$ represent the locally varying Kelvin-Voigt and Landau-Lifshitz dissipation terms, respectively. The analysis demonstrates that when these functions are piecewise constant, the system exhibits stable energy decay. This result extends previous findings by the authors, which addressed the case of globally defined $\alpha(x)$ and $\beta(x)$. Furthermore, the proof relies on a novel technique for handling the coupling term, which is expected to be applicable to other coupled hyperbolic systems. The methodology involves:
\begin{enumerate}
